WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.019
On the federal side, account management and
external personnel security call for the

2
00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:07.609
source decision, the
reconciliation report,

3
00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:11.738
and how long each contractor's access
took to block after their end date.

4
00:00:11.738 --> 00:00:14.629
Identifying each person
by status means the

5
00:00:14.629 --> 00:00:17.363
worker type code appears on every account.

6
00:00:17.363 --> 00:00:21.263
OMB's zero trust memo says
enterprise identity draws on HR,

7
00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:24.351
contract management
and personnel security,

8
00:00:24.351 --> 00:00:29.388
so the governance body signs a table
that names one authority for each fact.

9
00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:33.116
To validate, one kit check lists
enabled accounts with no key,

10
00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:36.025
which is where contractors
without one show up.

11
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:40.954
No check reads end dates, so the
evidence is the reconciliation re-run,

12
00:00:40.954 --> 00:00:43.375
with no contractor past their end.

13
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:46.053
In Azure Government, API-driven inbound

14
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:49.300
provisioning and access
reviews are available.

15
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.920
Until the contractor source is automated,

16
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.188
keep the contract end date as the
leave date so the leaver still fires.

17
00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.813
To roll back, pause the contractor app.

18
00:00:58.813 --> 00:01:00.140
It keeps its state.
